{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:00:10Z","created_by_operation":"op_b8071f0fb3da45d89865505b463104e4","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_1e1d0808139d05dba3864b86d25529872625311a4effe2d41a99e60192c16b84","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"clarisseio/python-agents@84c3bdc93ecd snapshot 45d89dabc1a851af","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_07d66e6655b4706b4a33c184f12e16c28f65c7b0c45e7fe26247964a55128b7f"],"source_ids":["src_f18ca62e82445030871acb4bf623017b"],"text":"The framework ships modules for agents, LLMs, prompt templating (Mustache-based), memory, tools, cache, errors, adapters, and logger, with agents and LLMs described as base classes defining common interfaces.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:00:10Z","updated_by_operation":"op_b8071f0fb3da45d89865505b463104e4"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:00:10Z","created_by_operation":"op_b8071f0fb3da45d89865505b463104e4","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_66b7a4cfb127b60833caf7c04e8539168c4f11e21546b810314e7ddcf9469ead","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"clarisseio/python-agents@84c3bdc93ecd snapshot 45d89dabc1a851af","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0110334e0896322f7e5cb225180a028eb71c9d01d19ff5784e7e394582548c78","slc_110f69352682445a84cb639d34c3f4ec9d7cbf822510a416ae7c93de57b8f9a7","slc_2230f81ad7e422583b14e88547c2da8152a5caf9ff0171747d870f9e39563f85","slc_3b5087bf8f7f486cf83531035f4911ebb72a2f13eaa2573730714db910397d89","slc_8f9f2267817e690642bd28c45f78445359c9b641ffabfd8538d538029390fc66","slc_bea208f64c3661ec1b84c121b254af10d196504da5746636c2c4ea5727265057","slc_f0a3c3c2d8cd08b14db55d823ae26335ac4cb95080cf1539b63827a60428c2ec","slc_fbee5b6ce5165173f6cc07724fcf59a1d96a93df2649ba6e1c5d3aa3f9f6c6fd"],"source_ids":["src_4e01e6e7cf245ddf92cb578eb0846fc4"],"text":"Caches expose async set/get/has/delete/clear/size operations, and custom caches are created by extending BaseCache, whose example also includes createSnapshot and loadSnapshot methods.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:00:10Z","updated_by_operation":"op_b8071f0fb3da45d89865505b463104e4"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:00:10Z","created_by_operation":"op_b8071f0fb3da45d89865505b463104e4","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8d53a7077166165c222faeffffa1630d57fb4c192fa056703e754080a92e1e81","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"clarisseio/python-agents@84c3bdc93ecd snapshot 45d89dabc1a851af","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_032f8c4db28911da92aeb1002c9fa67e760f1ac79284e7ea7a583f9d9d74c597","slc_733db3d7c057dedd78c2d52d529ed9c82e645bd89d060331bc037dd39d8b85ee","slc_7435f5131b5c6c47b18511385f99958b267acd8b91adaa95ce84a3018eb4cd8f","slc_a79c13909e128fd204137d12b813a719d18811c124dbd6c50504938d1f6785f4","slc_b2563e61b5da0a9b8666633985a4e87b667a51474cf914b08304934060097e1c"],"source_ids":["src_7fc872b5c47555819a045bc995aa3af0"],"text":"Memory classes such as UnconstrainedMemory store BaseMessage objects with add/addMany, expose messages, isEmpty, asReadOnly, and reset, and can be passed to LLM generate calls.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:00:10Z","updated_by_operation":"op_b8071f0fb3da45d89865505b463104e4"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:00:10Z","created_by_operation":"op_b8071f0fb3da45d89865505b463104e4","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_913dc7f704cc758ef9f4483e202bf62f82d35cb37c2e3ad7dfc780f94e846dd7","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"clarisseio/python-agents@84c3bdc93ecd snapshot 45d89dabc1a851af","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3fbf558d411e13e508901ada15666e43fd0671b6bbafb3aade93d0112a0a59c0","slc_8c5fe24ba04f7c4d5b0eec4bd5e47e9112e4cb0f5a3b021f82fdd7e13a0bfe01","slc_d858c842fe79db4829e01a9694c0ddce6543cbd06bd366e1d4384347d3dce87f"],"source_ids":["src_4e01e6e7cf245ddf92cb578eb0846fc4"],"text":"Cache keys are produced by serializing function parameters with key order irrelevant; the default decorator key function is ObjectHashKeyFn, and SingletonCacheKeyFn yields a single shared key regardless of arguments.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:00:10Z","updated_by_operation":"op_b8071f0fb3da45d89865505b463104e4"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:00:10Z","created_by_operation":"op_b8071f0fb3da45d89865505b463104e4","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_9c4e6d06d460d4142badf7aa52e19bce7e1bccf67582aff4296e4ed4dc407e4e","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"clarisseio/python-agents@84c3bdc93ecd snapshot 45d89dabc1a851af","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2acb2f2a86f38aeb0686adf63975de1cc5aec8aa0aecb6ae28dd2326d61aa209","slc_77c4e892c9f922a1b6ceec9845faeda4fc909a9623ce7615b13437c7efb0e498","slc_8a53f838565433e9275692e1b770ffcf4f7db28f56081670f01a24e1be7778e6"],"source_ids":["src_764ad1d0e96b5ceb8dffb452451711af","src_f18ca62e82445030871acb4bf623017b"],"text":"The run method supports an observe callback exposing an emitter where listeners can subscribe to events such as 'update' during execution; observe is also supported on tools and LLMs.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:00:10Z","updated_by_operation":"op_b8071f0fb3da45d89865505b463104e4"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:00:10Z","created_by_operation":"op_b8071f0fb3da45d89865505b463104e4","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_a8de7343144be5b87745fe02e08557bee254684a2e777138baec5ccf4c9f557a","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"clarisseio/python-agents@84c3bdc93ecd snapshot 45d89dabc1a851af","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_c67b37a900224e45929d69052a9aab2f5d3bdb55002d4a83315bfe70ab337885"],"source_ids":["src_f18ca62e82445030871acb4bf623017b"],"text":"The framework is designed to perform robustly with IBM Granite and Llama 3.x models, with optimization for other popular LLMs stated as ongoing work.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:00:10Z","updated_by_operation":"op_b8071f0fb3da45d89865505b463104e4"}
